# Goal Description

The goal is to implement 4 premium features (Voice Notes UI, Live Map Tracking, AI Predictive Quick-Chips, and Premium Animations/Glassmorphism) into the existing `ChatScreen.js` to make the Ustad AI application look more attractive and intelligent. The core backend orchestration logic and overall visual theme will remain exactly the same.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> We will need to install three new libraries to achieve these premium effects: `expo-blur` (for glassmorphism), `react-native-maps` (for the live tracking map), and `lottie-react-native` (for premium micro-animations). 
> **Are you okay with installing these packages?** (If you are testing on Expo Web, `react-native-maps` requires a fallback image instead of an interactive map. I will handle this automatically.)

## Proposed Changes

### mobile/src/screens/main/ChatScreen.js

#### [MODIFY] ChatScreen.js
- **Predictive Quick-Chips:** Add a horizontal `ScrollView` containing dynamic suggestion chips (e.g., "Emergency Plumber", "AC Maintenance") directly above the chat input bar. Clicking a chip will automatically populate the text input.
- **Voice Notes UI:** Modify the chat input bar. While the text is empty, the "Send" button will become a "Microphone" button. When pressed, it will show a visually pulsating "Listening..." state and simulate transcribing voice to text into the input field.
- **Live Map Tracking:** Update the `isLifecycleSimulation` logic so that when the "En-Route" message appears, it embeds a mini `MapView` (using `react-native-maps`) showing a fake route path approaching the user's location.
- **Glassmorphism & Lottie:** 
  - Wrap the Agentic Trace Log in a `BlurView` (`expo-blur`) for an iOS-style frosted glass effect.
  - Implement a `LottieView` checkmark animation inside the "Service Completed" message.

### package.json

#### [MODIFY] package.json
- Run `npx expo install expo-blur react-native-maps lottie-react-native` to add the required UI dependencies.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Restart the Expo server `npx expo start` to bundle the new native modules.
- Verify that `ChatScreen.js` compiles without layout breaks.

### Manual Verification
- Open the Chat Screen and verify the Predictive Chips scroll horizontally.
- Hold the Microphone button and verify it populates text.
- Execute a Booking and verify the `BlurView` looks premium and the Map renders correctly on the En-Route message without crashing Expo Go.
